  A summary of the results is that the validation error on the smaller hashgrid and FF MLP hyperparameters (to a point) was a lot better than the validation error on larger hashgrid and FF MLP hyperparameters as you can see a lot of the PSNR stayed around 28 dB. Furthermore, the hyperparameters for the SHdegree and `nFreq` didn't have much of a difference but did affect the time taken to train slightly. It also listed a lower learning rate of about $1^(-3)$ to be much stabler than the higher ones but large enough to learn/converge quickly. Finally, RelativeL2 had a lower loss than L2 and L1.

  The final "chosen" configuration based off of the validation testing is detailed in `validation_based_config.json`. /*!TODO: Create this initial config json file*/

  However, as will be seen in the next section, these results will appear misleading. Notes and a more detailed discussion about this is given in various `typst` files, but most prominently in `validation_error_explanation.typst`


]

